--------------------------------------------------
1. Project Structure
--------------------------------------------------

Photos81/
├─ src/
│  └─ photos/
│     ├─ Photos.java                (main JavaFX Application)
│     ├─ controller/
│     │  ├─ AdminController.java
│     │  ├─ AlbumsController.java
│     │  ├─ AlbumPhotosController.java
│     │  ├─ LoginController.java
│     │  └─ SearchController.java
│     ├─ model/
│     │  ├─ Album.java
│     │  ├─ Photo.java
│     │  ├─ Tag.java
│     │  ├─ User.java
│     │  └─ UserManager.java
│     └─ view/ (if used)
│        └─ *.fxml
├─ data/
│  ├─ stock_blue.png
│  ├─ stock_cyan.png
│  ├─ stock_gray.png
│  ├─ stock_green.png
│  ├─ stock_magenta.png
│  ├─ stock_red.png
│  └─ stock_yellow.png
│  └─ users.dat (created at runtime, NOT in repo)
├─ docs/
│  └─ index.html                    (generated Javadoc entry page)
├─ .gitignore
└─ README.txt 

Notes:
- data/users.dat is created at runtime and contains serialized users, albums,
  photos, and tags. It is not committed to the repository on purpose.

--------------------------------------------------
2. How to Run
--------------------------------------------------

1) Compile:

   javac --module-path "PATH_TO_FX/lib" --add-modules javafx.controls,javafx.fxml \
         -d bin $(find src -name "*.java")

2) Run:

   java --module-path "PATH_TO_FX/lib" --add-modules javafx.controls,javafx.fxml \
        -cp bin photos.Photos

Replace PATH_TO_FX with the actual JavaFX SDK location.

--------------------------------------------------
3. Users and Login
--------------------------------------------------

- Application uses username-only login (no passwords required).
- Special users:
  - admin  -> opens the admin subsystem.
  - stock  -> internal user that owns the base stock album.
- Any other username (e.g. user1, jo, etc.) opens the normal user subsystem.

On first run, UserManager auto-creates:
- admin user (no albums/photos).
- stock user with album “stock” and the 7 stock color photos.
- For every non-admin user, a “stock images” album populated with the same 7 stock photos.

All data is serialized into data/users.dat on logout or app exit and reloaded on next launch.

--------------------------------------------------
4. Features Implemented
--------------------------------------------------

1. Date of Photo
------------------

- Each Photo stores a java.time.LocalDateTime captured from the file’s last
  modification time.
- This value is read-only in the UI and shown as “Date” when viewing a photo.
- Date is used for:
  - Display in the album photo view.
  - Searching by date range.

2. Tags
---------

- Each photo has a collection of Tag objects (name, value).
- No duplicate (name, value) pairs are allowed on the same photo.
- Tag examples:
  - ("person", "Alice")
  - ("location", "New Brunswick")
- Tags can be:
  - Added via text fields (tag name + tag value).
  - Deleted via selection in the tag list.
- Multiple values for the same tag name (e.g., multiple “person” tags)
  are allowed as separate Tag objects.

3. Stock Photos & User Photos
-------------------------------

- data/ contains 7 low-resolution stock images, each a solid color:
  stock_red.png, stock_green.png, stock_blue.png, stock_yellow.png, etc.
- UserManager:
  - Ensures the stock user with album “stock” is always populated with these photos.
  - Ensures each non-admin user has a “stock images” album that also contains
    these photos.
- User photos:
  - Added via a FileChooser (BMP, GIF, JPEG, PNG).
  - The actual image files remain anywhere on the user’s machine.
  - The app stores only absolute file paths and metadata.
  - Paths are serialized into users.dat but not committed to GitHub.

4. Admin Subsystem
--------------------

Logging in as “admin” opens the admin screen:

- List all usernames.
- Create user:
  - Enter username and click “Add”.
  - UserManager.addUser ensures no duplicate usernames.
  - Non-admin users automatically receive a “stock images” album.
- Delete user:
  - Select a username and click “Delete”.
- Admin itself does not have albums or photos.
- Logout returns to the login screen.

5. Non-admin User Subsystem
-----------------------------

After logging in as a normal user:

- All existing albums for that user are loaded from users.dat.
- Initially displayed: Album list.

Each album row shows:
- Album name
- Number of photos
- Range of dates (earliest and latest photo date) for that album

Album Operations (Albums screen):

- Create album:
  - Enter new name, click “Add”.
  - Duplicate names are rejected per-user.
- Delete album:
  - Select and click “Delete”.
- Rename album:
  - Select album, enter new name, click “Rename”.
- Open album:
  - Opens the Album Photos screen for that album.
- Search:
  - Opens the Search screen.
- Logout:
  - Saves all data and returns to login.

Photo Operations (Album Photos screen):

- Left ListView:
  - Shows each photo with thumbnail + caption.
- Center display:
  - Large image preview.
  - Caption text field.
  - Date label (LocalDateTime).
- Right side:
  - Tag list and tag add/delete controls.

Supported actions:

- Add photo:
  - Uses FileChooser; prevents duplicate photo in the same album (same file path).
- Remove photo:
  - Removes from the current album only.
- Caption / recaption:
  - Edit caption and save.
  - Caption is shared across all albums containing that photo.
- Add tag / Delete tag:
  - Adds/removes tags on the selected photo.
  - Tag changes propagate to all albums containing that photo.
- Manual slideshow:
  - Prev and Next buttons step through photos in the album (wrap-around).
- Copy photo:
  - Prompts user for destination album name.
  - Adds the same Photo object to the destination album.
  - Edits to caption/tags are reflected in all albums.
- Move photo:
  - Same as copy, but also removes photo from the source album.

Search (Search screen):

1) Search by date range:
   - Choose From and To dates using DatePickers.
   - Shows all photos from all albums of the user whose date is in the range.

2) Search by tag(s):
   - Modes:
     - Single: one tag (name, value), e.g. person = Alice.
     - AND: intersection of two tag pairs, e.g. person=Alice AND location=New Brunswick.
     - OR: union of two tag pairs, e.g. person=Alice OR person=Bob.
   - Works correctly even when multiple values for the same tag name exist.

3) Create album from search results:
   - After a search, user can create an album containing all resulting photos.
   - Photos are not duplicated on disk; album just stores references to existing Photo objects.


--------------------------------------------------
5. Error Handling
--------------------------------------------------

- The console is never used for user-facing messages.
- All errors (invalid input, missing selection, I/O failures, etc.) are shown using
  JavaFX Alert dialogs.

Examples:
- “Album name cannot be empty.”
- “This photo is already in the album.”
- “Album does not exist.”
- “Select a photo/tag first.”

--------------------------------------------------
6. Javadoc
--------------------------------------------------

- Javadoc has been generated into the docs/ directory using:

  javadoc -d docs -sourcepath src -subpackages photos

- Open docs/index.html in a browser to view class and package documentation for:
  - photos.*
  - photos.controller.*
  - photos.model.*

